course: dictionary
lesson: 4667
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The words around a word, its context, tell you which meaning the writer wants. Hoist is a good example: it can mean lift something heavy, or raise a flag.
explain: «Hoist the sails!» shouts the captain, so hoist means pull something heavy up. Pirates «hoist the Jolly Roger» too, and that means raising their flag up a pole. Both meanings mean lifting something upwards, but one is for ropes and sails and one is for a flag.
explain: Hoist can also be a noun. A hoist is a machine that lifts heavy things or people, like the one a hospital uses to lift patients safely. Ask yourself: does my meaning fit this sentence? If it does, you have found the right one.
fact: Hoist can be a verb (to hoist something) or a noun (a hoist).
fact: To hoist means to lift or pull something heavy up, often with ropes or a machine.
fact: To hoist can also mean to raise a flag up a pole, or to lift yourself or someone else up.
fact: In science, pulleys help you hoist heavy loads with less effort.
fact: A hoist is a machine for lifting heavy things or people, such as in a hospital or care home.
exercise: «Hoist the sails!» What does hoist mean here? | *Pull the heavy sails up | Paint the sails blue | Sink the sails into the sea | Tear the sails down quickly
exercise: Dad «hoisted me onto his shoulders». What does hoisted mean? | Pushed me away | *Lifted me up | Carried me slowly across the road | Dropped me down
exercise: «The domestic storm-cone was hoisted», and a storm-cone is a warning signal hung up in harbours. What does hoisted mean? | Hidden under the water | Painted over | *Raised up | Broken into pieces
test: A hoist is a machine. What does it do? | Keeps you warm at night | *Lifts heavy things safely | Plays music loudly | Makes bread from flour
test: Pirates shouted «Hoist the Jolly Roger!». What did they do with the flag? | *Raised it up a pole | Folded it up small | Sold it at the market | Burned it on the deck
exam: In «Pulleys help hoist heavy loads with less effort», what does hoist mean? | *Lift up | Hide away | Fall asleep | Shout loudly
